      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied carolina-national-high-school.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Hand re-traced on 2026-10-08 from the owner image at enlarged scale: every distinguishable crown, canopy belt, lawn, planted bed, garden plot, hedge, path, apron, court and parking area is traced where the image shows it, and bare ground stays bare. Re-registered by hand (similarity fit, checks 0.4Ã¢â‚¬â€œ4.7 m). Mature canopy fills the campus between the classroom blocks: the belt between the red gym and the west road, the strip west of the long blue block, the clusters around the pale small block, the large group north of the central yard and the long belt south of the yard in front of the south classroom row, plus the strip behind the south-east blocks. The worn-earth central yard south of the pale block and the open dirt west of the long blue block stay bare. The corridor strip between the north row and the east blocks and the paved courts between the east classroom blocks are hardscape; the packed apron south of the gym runs to San IsidroÃ¢â‚¬â€œCarolina Road. Registration: hand similarity fit to hand-picked OSM roof corners and junctions; independent check errors 4.72 m, 0.44 m, 3.84 m. Trunks sit inside their observed crowns; crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships."
